JURISDICTION RULES
  USA : PD if published <= 1930 (95-year term); 1931-1977 = publication+95 with renewal/URAA caveat; >=1978 protected.
  EU  : PD if author died <= 1955 (life+70); if the author is unknown, publication+70 for anonymous works.
        death years come from VIAF, then the English Wikipedia; the
        Book-cell year is always the publication year.
  Statuses: public_domain | presumed_public_domain | in_copyright |
            presumed_in_copyright | unknown.  'presumed' always carries
            the reason in its *_basis column.
PIPELINE
  1 parse Book cell -> author/title/year/publisher
     the publication year is taken STRICTLY from this cell; it is the
     only year that feeds the rights rules
  2 query Google Books, Open Library, Crossref, Internet Archive
     (identity / licence evidence; their year goes to lookup_year only)
  3 resolve the first author's death year: VIAF first, Wikipedia second
     (the *name* may be completed from a strong catalogue match, but the
     death year itself comes only from those two sites)
  4 fuzzy-match candidates (title/author/year) and keep the best
  5 apply the US and EU rules to the Book-cell year (+ death year)
OUTPUT COLUMNS (appended to the input table)
  book_parse_type     citation | url | filename | archive_item | bibkey | junk | empty
  parsed_*            what step 1 extracted from the Book cell
  lookup_source       provider that supplied the accepted match (or 'none')
  lookup_match        matched title | authors | year
  match_score         0.55*title + 0.30*author + 0.15*year (+0.05 dictionary bonus)
  lookup_year         year printed by the catalogue -- REFERENCE ONLY, never used
  license             CC/public-domain licence URL reported by the source, if any
  author_death_year   first author's death year (VIAF, else Wikipedia) if found
  us_status / eu_status   verdicts; us_basis / eu_basis explain them
  rights_overall      combined verdict
  rights_confidence   high (Book-cell year corroborated) | medium (year from the cell) |
                      low (no year in the cell; death year only) | none
  access_evidence     provider access/licence flags (not a legal status)
  rights_notes        parse notes, year discrepancies, rejected death years

HOW TO READ THE LOG
  one block per row: PARSE -> QUERIES -> MATCHING -> DECISION -> [row time]
  everything is written even when a provider fails; failures never abort a row
